Planning rules

1. A daily revision budget must be configurable or use an existing study-duration preference.
2. Never silently exceed the configured budget.
3. Do not silently remove or overwrite existing Calendar tasks.
4. Do not assume an unavailable time slot is free.
5. Do not generate arbitrary exact start times without availability data.
6. If all due topics do not fit, prioritize them and show which remain unscheduled.
7. Make the remaining workload visible.
8. Allow the student to preview the plan before committing it to Calendar.
9. Recompute the preview when relevant inputs change.
10. Use stable ordering so the same inputs produce the same plan.

A due review must remain visible even if it does not fit within today's budget. Budget limitations should affect scheduling suggestions, not hide obligations.

Do not create an endless rescheduling loop where postponed tasks repeatedly duplicate themselves.

