13. REVISION SESSION WORKFLOW

Implement a complete review lifecycle.

Step 1 — Select a topic

The student selects a due topic or starts the highest-priority eligible review.

Step 2 — Review details

Show:

- Topic and subject.
- Why it is due.
- Last reviewed date, if available.
- Suggested revision duration, if available.
- A clear Start Review action.

Step 3 — Study

Where possible, launch the existing Focus timer with the correct revision context.

The student must also be able to study without a timer if the existing app supports such workflows.

Step 4 — Complete review

Require an explicit completion action. Do not mark completion merely because the timer ends or the student leaves the screen.

Step 5 — Record feedback

Offer Hard, Okay, or Easy feedback.

Explain the labels briefly and make the choice easy to understand.

If the student completes the session but skips feedback, preserve the completion if appropriate, but do not invent a rating. Apply the documented neutral or feedback-missing scheduling policy.

Step 6 — Update the engine

In one safe transaction where supported:

- Save the completed review event.
- Update the next due date.
- Update the interval and counters.
- Update derived state.
- Preserve the associated Focus session reference if valid.

Step 7 — Confirm the result

Show the next scheduled review date and a concise explanation of how the interval was determined.

Do not claim that the student has mastered the topic solely because they selected Easy.

